"""mojo_rt: the small runtime shim imported by code generated by rust-to-mojo.

Each module holds helpers for one Rust concept that has no exact Mojo
equivalent. Generated code imports names explicitly, for example
`from mojo_rt.num import rem`.

Modules:
  num     Rust integer/float semantics: truncated `%`, NaN-ignoring min/max,
          checked/saturating arithmetic, round-half-away-from-zero, float consts.
  option  Option helpers that return Optional instead of aborting.
  vec     Vec helpers with Rust return types (pop/get/first/last -> Optional).
  dict    HashMap helpers (remove -> Optional).
  cell    Cell / RefCell stand-ins (no dynamic borrow checking yet).
  range   RustRange, a value-level std::ops::Range.

Target: Mojo 1.0. This shim has NOT been compiled yet (no Mojo toolchain was
available when it was written); run scripts/check_mojo.sh on a Mojo machine.
"""
